{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"aa870cd0534b1d1fb899c72be85669782d6e44e36f36b5c13ea39966317e95db","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar_reconciler idempotency test harness","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py:311","binding_store_mod._now_iso","binding_lifecycle.py:45","binding_lifecycle.py:296","clear_absent","binding_lifecycle","binding_store","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py::test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence"],"problem_keywords":["idempotency","test oracle","clock mocking","module relocation","binding lifecycle","patch scope","integration test"],"propositions":["The idempotency oracle patches _now_iso only on binding_store_mod, but RP-02 S2 T2 moved clear_absent and siblings to binding_lifecycle, which resolves its own module-level _now_iso, so the patch no longer reaches those operations.","The integration test still passes because no-churn means the clock is never consulted on a healthy pass, but it would fail to catch a regression where clear_absent stamps updated_at unconditionally.","The unit-tier test test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence pins the no-stamp contract directly on the moved operations, so the coverage risk is contained.","Patching _now_iso on both binding_store and binding_lifecycle restores the integration oracle's original blast radius and regression detection capability."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787653128767611001,"uuid":"433cdfb9-545f-4119-95bb-fcfa6db717f1"}